import Rewriting.Rewrite

/-!
# Soundness of a rewrite system with respect to a model

A model of a rewrite system is an algebra in which every rule is valid: whenever a valuation
satisfies the conditions of a rule, both sides of the rule have the same value. The main result is
that rewriting then preserves values (`Steps.eval_eq`), i.e. the algebra is a model of the
equational theory generated by the rules.

For the mCRL2 sorts the model is the functional port itself: the carriers are the Lean types
(`Pos`, `Bool`, ...) and the operators are interpreted by the ported Lean functions, so the
soundness obligations are exactly the lemmas of `MachineNumbers.Proofs.*`.
-/

namespace Rewriting

variable {S : Signature} {V W : VarSet S} {ι : Type}

/-- `A` is a model of `R`: every rule is valid in `A` under every valuation satisfying its
conditions. -/
def Model (R : TRS S V ι) (A : Algebra S) : Prop :=
  ∀ (i : ι) (ν : Valuation A V),
    (∀ c ∈ (R i).conds, Term.eval A ν c.lhs = Term.eval A ν c.rhs) →
      Term.eval A ν (R i).lhs = Term.eval A ν (R i).rhs

end Rewriting
